@name Explainer 6: Rapid Rectilinear 50mm f/8
# Explainer #6: Rapid Rectilinear (Dallmeyer / Steinheil 1866): two
# identical cemented achromatic menisci (negative F2 flint outside,
# positive N-BK7 crown inside), symmetric about the stop, f/8.
# Role: symmetry cancels distortion and lateral colour (coma in part); the curved
# field (Petzval) remains.
# Design: the front half's curvatures, thicknesses and stop distance vary,
# mirrored to the rear half (EFL 50 mm; stop gaps >= 3 mm), minimising
# the white-light RMS spot at 0, 0.5, 0.7 and 1.0 of the field, object at
# 2.5 m.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/explainer/06-rapid-rectilinear.toml`.
# RMS spot (F, e, C) at f/8, object at 2.5 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 10.6, 0.5: 20.8, 0.7: 34.3, 1: 61.4 µm. Units: mm.
#
# radius      thickness   material       semi-diameter
  19.1203     5.3492      F2             5.770
  13.1070     2.2686      N-BK7          3.910
  33.5373     2.9999      air            3.680
  stop        2.9999      air            2.559
  -33.5373    2.2686      N-BK7          4.070
  -13.1070    5.3492      F2             5.200
  -19.1203    40.0000     air            6.250
